TI  - From AI Strategy to Executable Controls: A PRISMA-Guided Systematic Review of AI Governance for Cybersecurity Efficiency in Azerbaijan
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Cybersecurity, Digital Forensics, and AI Applications, ICCSDFAI 2026
SP  - 1261
EP  - 1267
DO  - 10.1109/ICCSDFAI70505.2026.11647955
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105049051679?origin=resultslist
AB  - The deployment of artificial intelligence across public-sector services, critical infrastructure, and national security operations creates an urgent demand for governance systems that can translate strategic principles into auditable, executable technical controls. This paper reports a completed PRISMA 2020 systematic literature review (n = 38; inter-rater reliability κ = 0.83) and derives from it a nine-pillar national AI governance control taxonomy tailored to Azerbaijan's legislative context. Each pillar is grounded in peer-reviewed evidence spanning responsible AI ethics, LLM security, MLOps governance, privacy-preserving computing, explainability, continuous monitoring, and agentic AI safety. All nine pillars are mapped to three operative national policy instruments - the AI Development Strategy 2025-2028, the Information Security and Cybersecurity Strategy 2023-2027, and the Law on Protection of Critical Information Infrastructure No. 949 - at the article level. Concrete technical implementation artefacts are proposed for each pillar together with five measurable operational efficiency KPIs, including Mean Time to Detect (MTTD ≤ 24 h) and Mean Time to Respond (MTTR ≤ 72 h), calibrated against CISA, ENISA, and NIST baselines and adjusted to reflect Azerbaijan's current SOC maturity and CII enforcement capacity. Cross-pillar dependency analysis and a structural comparison with the EU AI Act are also provided. The framework addresses a documented gap in post-Soviet AI governance scholarship by offering a replicable, evidence-based pathway from national AI strategy to operational cybersecurity control. © 2026 IEEE.
